# Prompt edits

Shared packs live in `prompts/<purpose>/prompt.md`. Collection overrides live in `collections/<topic>/prompts/`. Do not add a sixth artifact type (study guide, LinkedIn, competitive matrix, meeting notes) unless the owner asks for that output in the studio.

## Do not paste “super prompts”

Blog and social prompts are drafts, not packs. Steal at most one section heading or constraint. Do not copy use-case lists, Plus vs Free, Audio/Video feature ads, or claims about Gemini versions.

## Grounding (keep these)

- Use only notebook sources. No invented books, quotes, data, or page numbers.
- Cite **title and author**, not page/section numbers (ebooks and exports do not share pagination).
- Short quotes only, attributed. This repo is public; outputs are not a book dump.
- Label inferences. Omit what is not in the sources.
- Finance collections: no personal advice, no guaranteed-return language, no “what happens next” forecasts.

## When a change is allowed

Edit a pack only if a real export failed (ungrounded citations, fake consensus, trivia quiz, hype). Prefer tightening the existing numbered list over adding a new prompt file.

```md
# ❌ BAD — new pack from a blog
Create a Twitter thread and LinkedIn post from the paper.
Cite page numbers. Predict next year’s market.

# ✅ GOOD — one extra bullet on an existing pack
Flag where sources disagree; do not pick a winner unless the sources justify it.
```

If two purposes start to overlap (report vs quiz vs flashcards), keep one idea per pack. Duplicate study-guide structure is not an improvement.
